> The only thing I have left to try is NetBSD.

If it helps any I ran sdf.lonestar.org on 5305/1200s for a few years 
(NetBSD 1.5 to 1.6.1) excellently.  RCM via the serial console is 
excellent to have.  We've since moved to DS10Ls and CS20s.  Most of the
machines were auctioned off to members, but I still have one 5305/1200
with two CPUs and hopefully some RAM .. it should have 7 SBBs with 9.1GB
disks and it should boot up NetBSD 1.6.1

Make sure you have the latest SRM .. if you're going to netboot/bootp be
sure to have a DE500 (tulip/de) ethernet card.  Also, you'd need to use a
a symbios SCSI HA to boot off a disk (I use TEKRAM 575s (I think)).

They're still great machines.

